VW("hourly","overview","overview","The bank at the hour",{kind:"overview",mod:"hourbank",subs:[],eyebrow:"Hourly grain · overview",nrs:["hourly-story","grainfacts"],src:"granularity_hour 01–09",
 blocks:[M("hourbank",{subs:[]}),
 S("The direction","",'<p class="kicker">Replicate the whole process even where the synthetic generator leaves no signal. A documented set of non-trainable models is a result: each red gate names its root cause, the owner who must collect the missing data, and the test that proves a new feed delivers it.</p><p>The hour is where staffing, branch hours, send times and intraday fraud velocity live in a real bank. The same star, the same gates and one re-run command turn green as soon as real feeds arrive.</p>'),
 S("Nine notebooks","",'<div class="flow" id="hyFlow"></div>'),
 GF("hourly"),
 S("What the hour adds on this data","",'<div class="cards"><div class="card"><h4>No behavioural signal</h4><p class="small">No customer has a preferred hour, no channel has a rhythm, events inside a session come in random order, send-to-open delays are uniform over seven days.</p></div><div class="card"><h4>Validity controls</h4><p class="small">Only the hour can check opening hours, shifts and clocks, and all three fail.</p></div><div class="card"><h4>Operational clocks</h4><p class="small">Complaint assignment takes 3–22 h and first response 17–58 h (p10–p90); deadlines run in business hours.</p></div><div class="card"><h4>Streaming monitors</h4><p class="small">Hourly counts per market and channel with negative-binomial limits: a monitor, not a warehouse table.</p></div></div>')]});
